======================================================================
CONCLUSION: V is non-empty and positive-dimensional, but on EVERY
irreducible component (α, β) ≡ (0, 0). Therefore no atom from V
can contribute non-zero (α, β); the V-only strategy CANNOT produce
a 3-atom triple with (α, β)-rank 2.

Impossibility for the 'zero garbage' strategy: PROVEN.

The (2, 2, bridge-3) construction in any rank-1 atom family thus
requires garbage CANCELLATION across atoms (rank(U) ≤ 1 with U ≠ 0),
not zero garbage per atom.
